# Shreyas / Maya 1:1

Wednesday, October 7, 2026 at 09:01 · 18 min

## Attendees

- Shreyas
- Maya Chen

## Notes

#### Decisions

- Maya comes off the on-call rotation for the next two weeks, starting 7 October and returning on 21 October, with Shreyas as primary and Diego as secondary for sync.
- Maya takes Friday 9 October off.
- Maya is paused from phone screens until the end of the month but will do final-round interviews for the senior backend role.
- No contractor for the Microsoft side of Calendar Sync v2; hiring energy goes into the senior backend hire instead.
- Calendar Sync v2 dates hold (beta 13 November, GA 4 December); a Google-only beta is a fallback to revisit in two weeks, not the plan.
- The Microsoft subscription renewal design adds an hourly reconciliation sweep for unhealthy subscriptions and an alert when more than one percent of subscriptions are expired.
- The recurring-event test harness (moved occurrences, cancelled occurrences, series time zone changes) is part of Calendar Sync v2 scope.
- For customer-impacting incidents, Tom owns customer updates, Shreyas owns internal updates with an hourly cadence, and the person fixing it only talks in the incident channel.

#### Key facts

- **When does Calendar Sync v2 go to beta?** 13 November 2026, with GA on 4 December 2026.
- **What is the main risk on the Microsoft side of Calendar Sync v2?** Microsoft Graph webhook subscriptions for calendar events expire after roughly three days, so each technician's subscription must be renewed or Deino silently stops receiving that person's changes.
- **How will subscriptions be kept alive?** A renewal job every six hours that renews anything expiring in the next 24 hours, a handler for Microsoft lifecycle notifications, and a reconciliation sweep with delta queries (daily for everyone, hourly for unhealthy subscriptions).
- **When does Maya go back on call?** On 21 October 2026, after two weeks off the rotation.
- **Why did Shreyas not want a contractor?** Ramp-up time would run past the beta, any contractor with production access is in SOC 2 scope once the observation window opens on 1 November, and a Graph contractor costs fifteen to twenty thousand dollars a month when the senior backend role is already approved.
- **How many phone screens had Maya done recently?** Four in the last two weeks.
- **When would Maya's staff promotion take effect?** Realistically 1 January 2027, the start of the next quarter, after Aisha reviews Shreyas's promo doc.
- **What does Shreyas think Maya should grow in for staff?** Writing for people outside engineering, for example writing the next customer-facing postmortem.
- **What key does Calendar Sync now use to identify events?** The iCalUID plus the recurrence ID, for both Google and Microsoft.
- **How will Calendar Sync v2 cut over from polling for beta customers?** Five-minute polling keeps running alongside push; disagreements are logged and polling is trusted, and once the disagreement rate is near zero for a week polling drops to hourly as a safety net.
- **What did Shreyas tell Maya about the board meeting?** The board approved both hires (senior backend and mobile), Deino is not raising now, Series A conversations start in March, and runway is about nineteen months.
- **How much of the daily Google API quota does polling use?** About forty percent with five-minute polling; push should bring it under ten percent.

